     "tag": "Active Skill",
     "cost": 1,
     "action": "Action",
     "text": "Ouroboros Vigil reflects the search of understanding the origin and inner workings of the soul. With Replicant the Grimm User learns the ability to copy the essence of a soul into transmuter stones which create a new material know as a Soul Stone. The Grimm User then can use this Soul Stone to forge items that grants an ability known to the creature before it perished.\n\n#### Soul Stones.\nWhen a creature is reduced to 0 hit points and no more than 24 hours has passed since,  the Grim User can approach the corpse and try to analyze the creature's inner self. As an action the Grimm User makes a Harvest (int) Check against a DC equal to the **creature CR + 10** as long as the CR doesn't exceed the Max CR which is equivalent to the **Grimm User's Level + Its Prof. Bonus**. Creating a Soul Stone doesn't cost a Grimm Slot however it can only be attempted once per create as soul are fragile.\n___\nIf the Grimm User succeeds the harvest check it creates a Soul Stone of that creature with one trait of their choice, if the check is succeed by 10 or more it can choose two traits instead.\n___\nIf the Grimm User wishes, it can increment the Max CR by expending Grimm Slots while using this ability incrementing the Max CR by 1 per Grimm Slot used to a maximum of 3.\n___\nThere is a limit of Soul Stone that the Grimm User can carry before its own soul begins to be affected by the a more powerful presence. This limit is equivalent to twice the grimm user's intelligence modifier\n___\nSoul Stone Descriptions can be found on Soul Stones\n\n#### Soul Artifice\nOuroboros Vigil allows the Grimm User to harness the essence stored within a Soul Stone, forging powerful overlay items that integrate soul properties into them.\n___\nAs an `Action`, the Grimm User can expend a Grimm Slot and select a number of traits from their carried Soul Stones (which haven't been used) equal to their **Prof Bonus minus One per Each Active Soul Artifice Item (Min 1)**. Soul Artifice Items forged in this way have the following properties:\n\n- When using this ability, the Grimm user can choose the item to take the form of a weapon, armor or other equipment.\n\t\n- A item created assumes the base stats of the item (for each 5 levels the items gains a +1 Enhancement of type Weapon or Armor).\n\t\n- A Creature can only wield 1 of this Soul Artifice Items safely before it begins to interfere with the wielder's soul.\n\t\n- This items do not  require attunement and while carrying the item, the creature has access to its traits as if they were their own.\n\t\n- Items made with this ability last for 1 hour.\n\t\n- Items can be vanished at any time by the Grimm User.\n\t\n- The Grimm User is proficient with all Soul Artifice Items.\n\t\n___\nThis ability can also be used as a `Bonus Action` yet it doesn't guarantee that it will create an item with all features. After the first trait applied to the item the Grimm User must roll a intelligence check against a DC Equal to 5 times the number of additional traits applied to the item. (i.e. a item with four traits will require a Intelligence Check of DC 15). If failed the items is still created however with just the first trait.\n___\nAfter the Item is created it automatically is equipped by the Grimm User or an ally within a range of 15 x Prof Bonus ft."
