        "text": "While the Shift holds, Curse of the Ashes becomes **Scourge of the Ashes**, retaining all of its effects with these changes:\n- A creature can hold only **one Scourge** (not multiple Ash Curses), but there is **no limit** to the number of Scourges of the Ashes active across the battlefield at once.\n- **Ash Stacks become a shared pool** across all active Scourges, always equal to the **highest** among them; every Scourged creature is treated as holding that stack count. *(Explosion damage is unchanged: 1d10 per stack.)*\n- When the first Scourge is applied with none active, the shared pool **starts at your Dream Score Modifier** in stacks.\n- At the **end of each round**, the shared pool **increases by your Dream Score Modifier**.\n- Each **detonation** lowers the shared pool by your **Dream Score Modifier**.\n- The **bonus action** to raise Ash Stacks (per Curse of the Ashes) now raises the shared pool by your **Dream Score Modifier** instead of by 1.\n- The per-curse \"+1 attack / +1d8\" riders are replaced by a flat bonus scaling with level: **+6 (5th) / +9 (10th) / +12 (15th) / +15 (20th)** to your **attack rolls** and to the **damage of your hits** (flat, no dice)."
