     "id": "the-fallen-hero",
     "name": "The Fallen Hero",
     "text": "# The Fallen Hero\n\n*Umbra Platoon · White Rabbit · Commander: Grizzly*\n**Xeno Vorpidae — Knight-Captain of Acheron, The Ninety-Nine**\n\n![](img/troop_FallenHero.png)\n*\"He never talked about being afraid. He just checked that everyone else was okay first, and then he went.\"*\n\n**Role.** The first Vorpal Bunny, and the last one you call. He is not a specialization and cannot be assigned one — he arrives only through the Shackle Break **The Fallen Hero**, when someone is about to fall, and while he stands every other troop in the platoon kneels and takes his banner *(see **Knighted** on the Shackle Break)*.\n\n## Stats\n\n| Attribute | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Sigil** | ✦ |\n| **Role** | Knight-Captain · the one who stays |\n| **HP** | 120 + (12 × your level) |\n| **AC** | 22 |\n| **Speed** | 60 ft., climb 40 ft. |\n| **Charges** | The Collapse ×1 · Hold the Hour ×2 |\n\nUniversal traits and how the platoon is commanded are in **Umbra Platoon — Universal Traits**. He has all of them, and the following besides. **Last Stand does not apply to him** — see *The Ninety-Nine*.\n\n> [!note] DM — he is priced against a Divine Form, not against a Bulwark 🔒\n> This is a **Shackle Break's entire payload**, and the bar is The Parted Gates: a Divine Form at **CR = level + 10**, or a Defiled one at **+9 to every attack**. He holds the field for **three rounds**, once, for two Grimm Slots, 2 Exhaustion, 3 Dream Exhaustion and a bond that may not survive it. **He is supposed to be absurd.** If calling him is ever an arithmetic decision rather than an emotional one, he has been built wrong.\n\n## Traits\n\n**The Ninety-Nine.** He has died ninety-nine times. The hundredth is not today.\n\nWhile the Shackle Break holds, **damage cannot reduce him below 1 hit point**. Every blow that would drop him leaves him standing at 1, and he keeps going — no death saves, no Last Stand, no dying. He has done this before and he knows exactly how much of it he can take.\n\n*Nothing on the field can kill him. The clock can, and will, in three rounds.*\n\n**No One Else Falls.** This is the whole of him, and it reaches past the platoon.\n\nThe **first time** each round that any ally, troop or creature of your choice **within 60 ft.** would be reduced to 0 hit points, it is reduced to **1** instead and he is suddenly standing where it is. *Once per creature per Shackle Break.*\n\n**The One Who Goes First.** He acts on **your** initiative count whether or not you command the platoon, and he does not need the Umbra Platoon Bonus Action to move and act. He has **advantage on initiative**, opportunity attacks against him are made with **disadvantage**, and he cannot be surprised.\n\n**Knight-Captain.** Any troop within 10 ft. of him has **advantage on saving throws** and cannot be frightened. *(This is the banner — see **Knighted**.)*\n\n**Unfinished.** He cannot be charmed, turned, banished, polymorphed, stunned, paralyzed, or removed from the field by any effect that targets summons, conjurations or Grimm constructs — and he is immune to any effect that would end the Shackle Break early against your will. He is not being held here by the Grimm, and whatever *is* holding him is not finished with him.\n\n## Actions\n\n### Multiattack\n___\nThe Fallen Hero makes **three** Vorpal Blade attacks. On the round he arrives he makes these **immediately**, before anything else acts.\n\n### Vorpal Blade\n___\n*Melee Weapon Attack:* your **Dex modifier + Proficiency Bonus + your Proficiency Bonus again** to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. *Hit:* `Prof Bonus` d12s + your Dex modifier force damage.\n\n**Vorpal.** He scores a **critical hit on a roll of 18–20**. On a critical hit the target takes an **extra `Prof Bonus` d12s** force damage, and if the hit reduces a creature that is **not a Legendary creature** below a quarter of its hit point maximum, the blade finishes what the roll started: **it drops to 0 hit points.** Against a Legendary creature, a critical hit instead deals **maximum damage** on every die.\n\n*His crit range stacks with nothing — it does not add to, and is not added to, your Critical Range or any Critical Window.*\n\n### The Collapse\n*1 charge*\n___\nHe brings the ceiling down, the way he did in the eastern tunnels. Every creature of your choice in a **60-ft. cone** makes a **Dexterity saving throw** against **DC 8 + your Proficiency Bonus + your Dexterity modifier**, taking **10d10 bludgeoning damage** and being **knocked prone and restrained** on a failure, or half damage on a success. The area becomes **difficult terrain** until the Shackle Break ends, and the restrained can free themselves with a Strength check against the same DC.\n\n*He does not do this to kill anything. He does it to put stone between what is chasing you and you.*\n\n### Hold the Hour\n*2 charges*\n___\nHe takes out the unfinished watch and winds it. Every ally within 60 ft. — troops included — **regains hit points equal to your level + your Proficiency Bonus**, gains **temporary hit points equal to your level**, and **ends every condition** on itself from: blinded, charmed, deafened, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned, restrained and stunned.\n\n*Tick. Tick. Tick. The mechanism says: we are still here.*\n\n## Reactions\n\n### Stand Behind Me\n___\nWhen a creature within 60 ft. of him takes damage, he spends **his own Reaction** to put himself in the way: the damage is dealt **to him instead**, and he **halves it**. He may use this **three times per round**, and *The Ninety-Nine* means he can afford to.\n\n## Special — when he goes\n\n**He Kneels Once.** When the Shackle Break ends, before he goes, every creature of your choice within 120 ft. **regains hit points equal to twice your level**, and every ally that fell during the Shackle Break and has not been stabilised is **stabilised at 1 hit point**.\n\nHe checks that everyone else is all right first. He always did.",
