      "title": "Appendix: Trap Library",
      "text": "### Tier 1 — Basic Tactical Traps\n*Quantity: infinite.*\n\n#### Silken Snaptrap *(Proximity)*\n**Trigger:** an enemy enters the 5-ft square.\n- DC (15 + Prof) Dexterity save\n- **Fail:** Restrained and Silenced, 4d6 piercing + 4d6 force\n- **Success:** half damage, not restrained\n- **Restrained** until they pass a DC (15 + Prof) Strength check as an action, or another creature frees them with an action\n\n**Lvl 15+:** 20-ft radius of difficult terrain; 6d6 each; restrained creatures take 2d6 force at the start of their turns.\n**Lvl 20:** restrained creatures can only free themselves — no one else can.\n\n#### Mindwire Rune *(Spell Trigger)*\n**Trigger:** a spell is cast within 10 ft.\n- 6d8 psychic, no save\n- The caster makes a DC (15 + Prof) Intelligence save or is **Confused** for 1 round (as *confusion*)\n- The caster's **concentration breaks automatically**\n\n**Lvl 18+:** as a Bonus Action you may **store the spell** and name a Magus troop to cast it on its next turn, using your spell save DC and attack bonus.\n\n#### False Step Mine *(Movement Trigger)*\n**Trigger:** a creature Dashes, teleports, or is forcibly moved within 10 ft.\n- DC (15 + Prof) Constitution save\n- **Fail:** Blinded and Disarmed (drops held items), 3d10 thunder + 3d10 radiant\n- **Success:** half damage, Blinded until the end of its turn\n- Dropped items scatter 2d6 ft in random directions\n\n**Lvl 20+:** the triggering creature becomes **invisible to enemies only** for 1 round — you and your allies still see it.\n\n#### Spider's Reflection *(Aggression Trigger)*\n**Trigger:** an enemy within 15 ft targets you or a troop with an attack.\n- **Pulled 15 ft** toward the trap, no save\n- 4d8 slashing\n- DC (15 + Prof) Wisdom save or **Taunted** — it must target the same unit with its next attack; save ends\n\n**Lvl 16+:** also inflicts **Hex** for 1 minute; you hold it automatically and it doesn't count against your concentration.\n\n### Tier 2 — Advanced Strategic Traps\n*Quantity: 3 per Reality Shift.*\n\n#### Echoing Pitfall *(Melee Trigger)*\n**Trigger:** an enemy makes a melee attack within 5 ft.\n- The ground opens into a spectral burrow: DC (15 + Prof) Strength save or **fall into a dimensional pocket**\n- 4d6 bludgeoning + 4d6 psychic\n- **While fallen:** cannot act; attacks against it have advantage\n- It reappears at the start of its next turn in the nearest unoccupied space — you choose, if there is a choice\n\n**Lvl 15+:** 2 rounds, 6d6 each. **Lvl 19+:** you choose where it reappears, anywhere within 60 ft of the trap.\n\n#### Warren's Judgment *(Bloodied Trigger)*\n**Trigger:** an enemy within 15 ft drops below half HP.\n- Spectral rabbit warriors surge out of the shadows: **5d10 all-mighty damage**\n- DC (15 + Prof) Wisdom save or **Frightened** of the nearest troop for 1 minute, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns\n\n**Lvl 17+:** 8d10, and a spectral Vorpal Bunny distracts it — attacks against it have advantage until the start of its next turn.\n**Lvl 20:** the Frightened condition cannot be removed by any means inside the Shift.\n\n#### Loyal Chains *(Ally Damage Trigger)*\n**Trigger:** an ally within 15 ft takes damage.\n- Ethereal silk lashes the attacker for **half the damage dealt** as cognitive force damage — no save, and it cannot be reduced\n- DC (15 + Prof) Charisma save or **pulled 10 ft toward the trap and knocked prone**\n- **Chained:** speed reduced by 10 ft for 1 round, stacking with further triggers\n\n**Lvl 16+:** the injured ally also gains **temporary HP equal to half the damage taken** and **resistance to all damage** until the end of its next turn.\n\n#### Spore Burst *(Death Trigger)*\n**Trigger:** any creature dies within 10 ft.\n- A 20-ft cloud of toxic fungal spores: DC (15 + Prof) Constitution save for every enemy inside\n- **Fail:** 4d8 poison + 4d8 necrotic, **Poisoned** for 1 minute\n- **Success:** half damage, Poisoned until the end of its next turn\n- The area is **heavily obscured** for 1 round; the save repeats at the end of each turn\n\n**Lvl 15+:** 6d8 each, cloud lasts 2 rounds. **Lvl 18+:** the Poisoned also have disadvantage on attacks and cannot take reactions.\n\n### Tier 3 — Elite Queen's Traps\n*Quantity: 1 per Reality Shift.*\n\n#### Queen's Decree *(Critical Trigger)*\n**Trigger:** an enemy within 30 ft scores a critical hit.\n- **Teleported to the trap**, no save, and cocooned in webbing\n- **Restrained for 2 rounds**, which nothing but an effect that removes Restrained can end early\n- **6d10 cognitive force** at the start of each of its turns while cocooned\n- A DC (18 + Prof) Strength check as an action to break out, at disadvantage from the webbing\n- **While cocooned** it is vulnerable to all damage from you and your troops\n\n**Lvl 18+:** 3 rounds, 8d10 per turn. **Lvl 20:** it cannot use Legendary Resistances or Legendary Actions, and every attack against it is a critical hit.\n\n#### Acheron's Gaze *(Ability Trigger)*\n**Trigger:** an enemy within 30 ft uses a Legendary Action, a Legendary Resistance, or a class capstone.\n- Eight spectral spider eyes open above it: **DC (17 + Prof) Wisdom save**\n- **Fail:** **Paralyzed** for 1 round, 8d10 all-mighty damage\n- **Success:** **Stunned** until the end of its turn, half damage\n- Either way **the ability is still spent**. A creature with truesight has disadvantage on the save — it sees the Queen's true form\n\n**Lvl 19+:** Paralyzed 2 rounds, 10d10. **Lvl 20:** Legendary Resistance cannot avoid it — it is spent and the effect lands anyway."
