 "realityShift": "*Grimm Feature (Unlocked at Unveiling Stage)*\n___\n\nA **Reality Shift** allows a Grimm User to superimpose their **Dream Node** onto the world, transforming the battlefield into a realm shaped by their subconscious. Within this dream space, the laws of reality bend to the will of the Grimm and its User.\n\n---\n\n## Activation Requirements\nTo activate a Reality Shift, the Grimm User must meet the following conditions:\n- The Grimm must have reached its **Second Awakening** called Unveiling.\n- The User must possess **Dream Affinity 1 or higher**.\n- The User must use a **Natural Turn Action** that cannot be downgraded and cannot be under the **restrained** condition.\n- The User **must not have any levels of Dream Exhaustion**.\n\n---\n\n## Core Rules of Reality Shift\n\n| Rule #                             | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| ---------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **1. Duration**                    | The Reality Shift lasts **1 minute (10 rounds)**, or ends early if the Owner falls **unconscious**, or **ends it as a bonus action**.                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| **2. Pocket Plane Creation**       | A Dream Node manifests. All creatures currently in initiative are **trapped** within.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| **3. Escape Attempt**              | A trapped creature can move to the edge and attempt an **Incept Check**: - **DC = 20 + Owner's Dream Modifier + Proficiency Bonus**. - **Success:** The creature escapes. - **Failure:** The creature remains trapped and cannot attempt to Escape until the end of its next turn.  This rule apply to all Reality Shift without an Exit Condition |\n| **4. Critical Openings**           | Each **critical hit** against the Owner **lowers the Escape DC by 2** (cumulative).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| **5. Lair Action**                 | The Owner gains a **Lair Action** at **Initiative 20** (loses ties). This action is unique to their Grimm and Reality Shift. A Lair Action can also be exchanged for available Action or Bonus Action of the Owner.                                                                                                                                               |\n| **6. Auto-Hit Reality**            | The Owner’s **attack rolls automatically hit** within the Reality Shift if they can reach the target. Rolls must still be made to determine **critical hits**.                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| **7. Grimm Slot Recovery**         | The Owner **recovers 2 Grimm Slots** at the **start of their turn**. They **cannot exceed their maximum**.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| **8. Collapse on Unconsciousness** | If the Owner is reduced to **0 HP**, the Reality Shift ends **immediately** and the Collapse Effect takes place.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| **9. Reentry Lockout**             | Creatures who **escape** the Reality Shift **cannot re-enter** or be affected by internal effects.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| 10. Complete Loadout               | While inside the Reality Shift, the Grimm User gains temporary access to **all Additional Grimm Abilities** listed in their Grimm’s entry, regardless of whether they’ve been selected or previously unlocked.  These abilities are only available while the Reality Shift is active and are lost once it ends.                                          |\n| **11. Exhaustion Cost**            | When the Reality Shift ends, the Owner gains **3 points of Exhaustion** and **5 points of Dream Exhaustion**.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| **12. Cooldown**                   | The Grimm User cannot use Reality Shift again for **720 in-game hours (30 days)**.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| **13. Dreamified Challenge**       | While the Reality Shift is active, any time a creature needs to make a Saving Throw against a Owner's, the DC increases by their Dream Score Modifier.                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n\n---\n\n## Reality Clash\n\nWhen multiple Grimm Users activate their Reality Shift simultaneously or while inside another’s, a **Reality Clash** begins.\n\n- To initiate, a Grimm User attempts a **contested Incept Check** against the current Owner.\n- On a success, a **Reality Clash** begins, and control **shifts each round** between the participants at the start of their turn.\n- On a failure, the challenger may try again on a later turn.\n\n### Clash Effects:\n- **Rules #4 (Critical Openings), #5 (Lair Action), and #6 (Auto-Hit)** are **disabled** during the Clash.\n- A **Grimm User** only benefits from their Reality Shift effects on their turn.\n- The Reality Clash ends when only one Grimm User remains conscious with an active Shift, reclaiming full control.\n\n---\n\n> **Reminder:** Each Reality Shift is **unique** to the Grimm and its User, with custom terrain, effects, and narrative theming. The above rules define the **shared structure** of this powerful ability.",
