   "text": "*Soul Stone*\n___\nThe soul of a sorcerer preserved into a stone flourishing with the following features:\n\n### Meta Magic\n*Passive Feature*\n___\nThe Meta Magic feature grants 25 sorcery points, which it can spend to fuel **sorcerer** spells and various metamagic effects:\n* ***Quickened Spell.*** The Sorcerer can cast a spell that has a casting time of 1 action as a bonus action by spending 2 sorcery points.\n* ***Heightened Spell.*** When the Sorcerer casts a spell that forces a creature to make a saving throw to resist its effects, it can spend 3 sorcery points to give one target of the spell disadvantage on its first saving throw made against the spell.\n\n### Sorcerer Spirit\n*Soul Chimera*\n___\nBy using the Soul Stone for a Soul Chimera, you can assume the powers of the Sorcerer Spirit",
   "spirit": "Sorcerer Spirit",
   "spiritText": "*Medium Replica, Neutral*  \n___\n- **Armor Class** 15 (Mage Armor)  \n- **Hit Points** 44 (6d6 + 12)  \n- **Speed** 30 ft.  \n___\n\n| STR     | DEX     | CON     | INT     | WIS     | CHA     |\n|:-------:|:-------:|:-------:|:-------:|:-------:|:-------:|\n| 10 (+0) | 14 (+2) | 14 (+2) | 12 (+1) | 12 (+1) | 18 (+4) |\n___\n- **Saving Throws** Con +5, Cha +7  \n- **Skills** Deception +7, Intimidation +7, Stealth +4  \n- **Damage Resistances** Necrotic  \n- **Senses** Darkvision 120 ft., Passive Perception 11  \n- **Languages** Common, Abyssal  \n- **Challenge** 8  \n___\n\n**Shadow Magic – Strength of the Grave.** When damage reduces the Sorcerer Spirit to 0 hit points, it can make a DC 5 + the damage taken Charisma saving throw. On a success, it instead drops to 1 hit point. This feature doesn't work if the damage is radiant or from a critical hit.\n\n### Actions\n***Spellcasting.*** The Sorcerer Spirit is a 6th-level spellcaster. Its spellcasting ability is Charisma (spell save DC 15, +7 to hit with spell attacks). It knows the following spells:\n\n**Cantrips (at will):** *Chill Touch, Minor Illusion, Mage Hand, Prestidigitation, Fire Bolt*  \n**1st level (4 slots):** *Shield, Mage Armor, Disguise Self*  \n**2nd level (3 slots):** *Darkness, Mirror Image*  \n**3rd level (3 slots):** *Counterspell, Fear*  \n**4th level (1 slot):** *Greater Invisibility*\n\n___\n\n### Shadow Sorcerer Features\n\n***Eyes of the Dark.*** The Sorcerer Spirit can see through darkness, both magical and nonmagical, out to a range of 120 feet.\n\n***Hound of Ill Omen (1/Short Rest).*** As a bonus action, the Sorcerer Spirit can spend 3 sorcery points to summon a spectral hound to target one creature within 120 feet. The hound uses the **Dire Wolf's** statistics, with the following changes:  \n- It is size Medium and appears ghostly.  \n- It can move through creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain. The hound takes 5 (1d10) force damage if it ends its turn inside an object.  \n- The hound appears within 30 feet of the target, moves toward it by the most direct route on its turns, and has advantage on attack rolls against it.  \n- If the target is killed, the hound disappears at the end of the Sorcerer Spirit’s next turn.\n\n***Shadow Walk.*** As a bonus action, the Sorcerer Spirit can teleport up to 120 feet to an unoccupied space it can see that is in dim light or darkness.\n\n### Sorcery Points (6/Long Rest)\nThe Sorcerer Spirit has 6 sorcery points, which it can spend to fuel various metamagic effects:\n\n- ***Quickened Spell.*** The Sorcerer Spirit can cast a spell that has a casting time of 1 action as a bonus action by spending 2 sorcery points.  \n- ***Twinned Spell.*** When casting a spell that targets only one creature and doesn’t have a range of self, the Sorcerer Spirit can target a second creature within range by spending a number of sorcery points equal to the spell’s level."
